WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.340
Two test tubes stand in
a beaker of hot water.

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:08.500
One holds propanal, the other propanone,
but we won't say which is which.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.820
Both have three carbons and a
carbon to oxygen double bond.

4
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.540
Tollens' reagent goes into each tube.

5
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.740
Soon, the glass of one
tube turns into a mirror.

6
00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.340
In the other tube, nothing changes.

7
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.800
Same double bond, same reagent.

8
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.940
So why does only one of them
coat the glass with silver?

9
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:32.780
In this mission, you'll learn the test-tube
tests that tell aldehydes and ketones apart.

10
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:37.820
Then you'll put the results together,
step by step, to name an unknown compound.

11
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.450
Your mission: explain why only one of
these compounds makes a silver mirror.